2
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:30,000
Terminator Genisys is a science fiction, action,
thriller film directed by Alan Taylor.

3
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:42,000
The year is 2029.

4
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:54,000
John Connor, leader of the resistance continues the war against the machines.

5
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:06,000
At the Los Angeles offensive, John's fears of the unknown future begin to emerge when TECOM spies reveal a new plot by
SkyNet that will attack him from both fronts; past and future, and will ultimately change warfare forever.

6
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:18,000
Sarah Connor, played by Emilia Clarke.

7
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:30,000
Kyle Reese, played by Jai Courtney.

8
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:42,000
Guardian / The Terminator, played by Arnold Schwarzenegger.

9
00:37:48,000 --> 00:37:54,000
John Connor, played by Jason Clarke.

10
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Alex / Skynet, played by Matt Smith.

11
00:46:12,000 --> 00:46:18,000
O'Brien, played by J.K. Simmons.

12
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:30,000
Terminator Genisys is a 2015 American science fiction action film serving as a
reboot and the fifth installment in the Terminator franchise.

13
00:54:36,000 --> 00:54:42,000
Directed by Alan Taylor from a screenplay by Laeta Kalogridis and Patrick Lussier, the film stars Arnold
Schwarzenegger reprising his role as the Terminator, alongside Jason Clarke, Emilia Clarke, Jai Courtney, J.

14
00:58:48,000 --> 00:58:54,000
Simmons, and Lee Byung-hun.

15
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
Despite Schwarzenegger's involvement and the mirroring of certain events from the previous films, the film is a standalone entry
with no canonical connection to the prior installments; it is described as a "reimagining" of The Terminator (1984).

16
01:07:12,000 --> 01:07:18,000
The plot follows Kyle Reese (Courtney), a soldier from a
post-apocalyptic 2029 where humanity wages war against Skynet.

17
01:11:24,000 --> 01:11:30,000
Sent back to 1984 to protect Sarah Connor (Emilia Clarke), Reese discovers the timeline has been
altered—Sarah was raised by a reprogrammed Terminator (Schwarzenegger) sent to guard her.

18
01:15:36,000 --> 01:15:42,000
The film explores the consequences of Skynet's
interference with temporal events.

19
01:19:48,000 --> 01:19:54,000
Development began after the Halcyon Company, then-owners of the franchise, filed for
bankruptcy following the underperformance of Terminator Salvation (2009).

20
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
Megan Ellison's Annapurna Pictures acquired the rights in 2011,
partnering with her brother David's Skydance Productions.

21
01:28:12,000 --> 01:28:18,000
However, Annapurna dropped their involvement, although Megan
still retained executive producer credit.

22
01:32:24,000 --> 01:32:30,000
The producers consulted original creator James Cameron and drew
inspiration from the first two Terminator films.

23
01:36:36,000 --> 01:36:42,000
Principal photography occurred mainly in New Orleans and San Francisco, with visual
effects handled by six companies and practical effects by Legacy Effects.

24
01:40:48,000 --> 01:40:54,000
Premiering at the Dolby Theatre on June 28, 2015, and released widely on July 1, the film was largely panned
by critics for its plot, though some praised the action sequences and Schwarzenegger's return.

25
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:06,000
It grossed $440.6 million worldwide, making it the franchise's second-highest-grossing entry
after Terminator 2: Judgment Day, yet it underperformed relative to expectations.

26
01:49:12,000 --> 01:49:18,000
Planned sequels and a TV spin-off were cancelled, though a video game,
Terminator Genisys: Future War, was released in 2017.

27
01:53:24,000 --> 01:53:30,000
The franchise continued with Terminator: Dark Fate
(2019), a direct sequel to Terminator 2.

28
01:57:36,000 --> 01:57:42,000
The film explores themes of future, artificial intelligence
(a.i.), saving the world, cyborg, killer robot.

29
02:01:48,000 --> 02:01:54,000
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
